#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:637
msgid "Vector Support"
msgstr "Stöd för vektorer"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:639
msgid ""
"*Vectors* (points, colors, or 3D vectors) may be intermixed with *scalars* "
"(simple floating point values).  If a scalar is used in a vector context, it "
"is replicated into the three components, e.g. ``0.5`` becomes ``[0.5, 0.5, "
"0.5]``."
msgstr ""
"*Vektorer* (punkter, färger eller tredimensionella vektorer) kan blandas "
"fritt med *skalärer* (enkla flyttalsvärden).  Om en skalär används i ett "
"vektorsammanhang, replikeras den till de tre komponenterna, t.ex. ``0.5`` "
"blir ``[0.5, 0.5, 0.5]``."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:643
msgid ""
"If a vector is used in a scalar context, only the first component is used. "
"One of the benefits of this is that all the functions that are defined to "
"work with scalars automatically extend to vectors.  For instance, ``pick``, "
"``choose``, ``cycle``, ``spline``, etc., will work just fine with vectors."
msgstr ""
"Om en vektor används i ett skalärt sammanhang, används bara den första "
"komponenten. En av fördelarna med det är att alla funktioner som är "
"definierade att fungera med skalärer automatiskt utökas till vektorer  "
"Exempelvis fungerar ``pick``, ``choose``, ``cycle``, ``spline``, etc., "
"utmärkt med vektorer."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:649
msgid ""
"Arithmetic operators such as ``+``, ``*``, etc., and scalar functions are "
"applied component-wise to vectors.  For example, applying the ``gamma`` "
"function to a map adjusts the gamma of all three color channels."
msgstr ""
"Aritmetiska operatorer såsom ``+``, ``*``, etc. och skalära funktioner "
"appliceras per komponent på vektorer. Genom att exempelvis applicera "
"``gamma`` funktionen på en avbildning justerar gamma för alla tre "
"färgkanalerna."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:655
msgid "Curve Functions"
msgstr "Kurvfunktioner"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:657
msgid ""
"Interpolation of parameter values to a set of control points is governed by "
"the following functions."
msgstr ""
"Interpolering av parametervärden till en uppsättning styrpunkter regleras av "
"följande funktioner."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:661
msgid ""
"color **ccurve** ( float param, float pos0, color val0, int interp0, float "
"pos1, color val1, int interp1, [...] )"
msgstr ""
"color **ccurve** ( float param, float pos0, color val0, int interp0, float "
"pos1, color val1, int interp1, [...] )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:663
msgid ""
"Interpolates color ramp given by control points at ``param``. Control points "
"are specified by triples of parameters ``pos_i``, ``val_i``, and "
"``interp_i``."
msgstr ""
"Interpolerar en färgramp given av styrpunkter i ``param``. Styrpunkter anges "
"av tripplar av parametrarna ``pos_i``, ``val_i``, och ``interp_i``."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:668 ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:682
msgid "Interpolation codes are:"
msgstr "Interpolationskoder är:"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:670 ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:684
msgid "0 - none"
msgstr "0 - ingen"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:671 ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:685
msgid "1 - linear"
msgstr "1 - linjär"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:672 ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:686
msgid "2 - smooth"
msgstr "2 - jämn"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:673 ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:687
msgid "3 - spline"
msgstr "3 - spline"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:674 ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:688
msgid "4 - monotone (non-oscillating) spline"
msgstr "4 - monoton (icke-oscillerande) spline"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:675
msgid ""
"float **curve** ( float param, float pos0, float val0, int interp0, float "
"pos1, float val1, int interp1, [...] )"
msgstr ""
"float **curve** ( float param, float pos0, float val0, int interp0, float "
"pos1, float val1, int interp1, [...] )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:677
msgid ""
"Interpolates a 1D ramp defined by control points at ``param``. Control "
"points are specified by triples of parameters ``pos_i``, ``val_i``, and "
"``interp_i``."
msgstr ""
"Interpolerar en endimensionell ramp definierad av styrpunkter i ``param``. "
"Styrpunkter anges av tripplar av parametrarna ``pos_i``, ``val_i``, och "
"``interp_i``."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:689
msgid ""
"float **spline** ( float param, float y1, float y2, float y3, float y4, "
"[...] )"
msgstr ""
"float **spline** ( float param, float y1, float y2, float y3, float y4, "
"[...] )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:691
msgid ""
"Interpolates a set of values to the parameter specified where ``y1``, ..., "
"``yn`` are distributed evenly from ``[0, 1]``."
msgstr ""
"Interpolerar en uppsättning värden till angiven parameter där ``y1``, ..., "
"``yn`` är likformigt distribuerade från ``[0, 1]``."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:696
msgid "Custom Plugins"
msgstr "Egna insticksprogram"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:698
msgid ""
"Custom functions may be written in C++ and loaded as one or more dynamic "
"plugins.  See `Writing Custom Expression Plugins <https://wdas.github.io/"
"SeExpr/doxygen/plugins.html>`_ for more details."
msgstr ""
"Egna funktioner kan skrivas i C++ och läsas in som ett eller flera dynamiska "
"insticksprogram. Se `Writing Custom Expression Plugins <https://wdas.github."
"io/SeExpr/doxygen/plugins.html>`_ för mer detaljerad information."

